.TH RICHCHAR 1 "August 2026" "Richchar 1.1.0" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
richchar \- local-first talking portrait generator
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B richchar
--image IMAGE
(--text TEXT | --script-file FILE)
--voice-model MODEL
--output FILE
.RI [ options ]
.SH DESCRIPTION
Richchar orchestrates Piper, Wav2Lip GAN, GFPGAN, and FFmpeg to create talking portrait videos.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.B --image FILE
Source portrait.
.TP
.B --text TEXT
Narration text.
.TP
.B --script-file FILE
Read narration from a text file.
.TP
.B --voice-model FILE
Piper ONNX voice model.
.TP
.B --output FILE
Destination MP4.
.TP
.B --preview-seconds N
Create a short preview.
.TP
.B --resume
Resume supported intermediate work.
.TP
.B --box TOP BOTTOM LEFT RIGHT
Supply a manual face box.
.TP
.B --doctor
Check dependencies and configured paths.
.TP
.B --help
Display help.
.SH QUALITY
The validated GFPGAN baseline uses GFPGANv1.4, upscale 1, clean architecture, center-face restoration, paste-back enabled, and weight 0.65.
Final video uses libx264, CRF 14, and preset slow.
.SH LIMITATIONS
Version 1.1.0 targets photographic human portraits. Cartoon and heavily illustrated faces are not validated quality targets.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR ffmpeg (1),
.BR python3 (1)
